1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,680
Three days in Seoul.

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:03,780
Palaces, markets

3
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:05,680
a city view at sunset

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,740
and one day that's completely yours.

5
00:00:09,306 --> 00:00:11,092
If this is your first time

6
00:00:11,092 --> 00:00:13,665
this plan keeps each day in one part of

7
00:00:13,665 --> 00:00:14,295
the city

8
00:00:14,295 --> 00:00:16,711
so you spend your time looking around

9
00:00:16,711 --> 00:00:17,971
not changing trains.

10
00:00:17,971 --> 00:00:20,440
I'll show you the route for every day

11
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:21,280
what to eat

12
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:25,046
and the small mistakes that trip up first-time visitors.

13
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:28,000
Let's start with a few things to sort out

14
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,880
before day one.

15
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:31,330
First

16
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:33,390
check your dates.

17
00:00:33,390 --> 00:00:36,350
Gyeongbokgung Palace is closed on Tuesdays

18
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:39,710
and Changdeokgung Palace is closed on Mondays.

19
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:41,470
If your trip falls that way

20
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:43,890
just swap day one and day three.

21
00:00:44,208 --> 00:00:45,308
Second

22
00:00:45,308 --> 00:00:48,108
get a transit card when you arrive.

23
00:00:48,108 --> 00:00:50,368
You tap it on the subway and on buses

24
00:00:50,368 --> 00:00:53,748
and transfers within a short time are discounted.

25
00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:54,643
Third

26
00:00:54,643 --> 00:00:56,594
install Naver Map or KakaoMap.

27
00:00:56,594 --> 00:00:59,303
Google Maps can show you places in Korea

28
00:00:59,303 --> 00:01:01,308
but its directions are limited

29
00:01:01,308 --> 00:01:03,746
so a Korean map app will save you a

30
00:01:03,746 --> 00:01:05,130
lot of guessing.

31
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:07,780
Flying into Incheon?

32
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:10,820
The AREX airport train is the simplest way

33
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:12,640
into central Seoul

34
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:15,580
and airport buses and taxis are good options

35
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:19,160
if you have heavy bags or arrive late.

36
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,660
Pick whichever drops you closest to your hotel.

37
00:01:22,086 --> 00:01:24,826
And where should you stay?

38
00:01:24,826 --> 00:01:27,526
Central Seoul works best for this plan.

39
00:01:27,526 --> 00:01:29,646
Around Gwanghwamun, Jongno

40
00:01:29,646 --> 00:01:31,486
City Hall or Myeongdong

41
00:01:31,486 --> 00:01:34,146
every stop is a short subway ride or a

42
00:01:34,146 --> 00:01:34,766
walk away.

43
00:01:35,352 --> 00:01:38,192
Day one is all about old Seoul

44
00:01:38,192 --> 00:01:41,072
and you can do the whole day on foot.

45
00:01:41,562 --> 00:01:44,522
Start early at Gyeongbokgung Palace

46
00:01:44,522 --> 00:01:47,482
the largest of Seoul's royal palaces from the

47
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:49,082
Joseon dynasty.

48
00:01:49,082 --> 00:01:52,322
Get off at Gyeongbokgung Station on Line 3.

49
00:01:52,322 --> 00:01:54,562
If you arrive around opening time

50
00:01:54,562 --> 00:01:57,222
the big courtyards are much quieter.

51
00:01:57,828 --> 00:02:00,688
The changing of the royal guard at Gwanghwamun

52
00:02:00,688 --> 00:02:03,588
Gate usually happens at ten in the morning and

53
00:02:03,588 --> 00:02:05,608
two in the afternoon.

54
00:02:05,608 --> 00:02:07,108
And here's a fun one:

55
00:02:07,108 --> 00:02:08,608
if you wear hanbok

56
00:02:08,608 --> 00:02:10,148
the traditional dress

57
00:02:10,148 --> 00:02:12,688
entry to the palaces is free.

58
00:02:12,688 --> 00:02:15,048
There are rental shops near the station.

59
00:02:15,678 --> 00:02:18,418
Give the palace about two hours.

60
00:02:18,418 --> 00:02:22,058
Then walk east to Anguk and the hanok lanes

61
00:02:22,058 --> 00:02:23,478
of Bukchon.

62
00:02:23,478 --> 00:02:24,778
These are real homes

63
00:02:24,778 --> 00:02:28,558
so keep your voice down and stay out of doorways.

64
00:02:28,558 --> 00:02:30,818
Some parts of Bukchon now have visiting hours

65
00:02:30,818 --> 00:02:32,098
for tourists

66
00:02:32,098 --> 00:02:34,158
so check the signs as you go.

67
00:02:34,632 --> 00:02:36,812
When your feet need a rest

68
00:02:36,812 --> 00:02:38,532
Anguk is full of cafes

69
00:02:38,532 --> 00:02:40,792
and some are inside old hanok houses with

70
00:02:40,792 --> 00:02:43,032
wooden beams and little courtyards.

71
00:02:43,032 --> 00:02:44,452
Order at the counter

72
00:02:44,452 --> 00:02:46,912
and it's normal to sit as long as you like.

73
00:02:47,394 --> 00:02:48,559
In the afternoon

74
00:02:48,559 --> 00:02:51,056
head a few minutes south to Insadong.

75
00:02:51,056 --> 00:02:54,052
The main street and its side alleys are full

76
00:02:54,052 --> 00:02:55,495
of traditional crafts

77
00:02:55,495 --> 00:02:57,548
tea houses and small galleries.

78
00:02:57,548 --> 00:03:00,100
It's a good place for small souvenirs

79
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,954
like hanji paper goods.

80
00:03:02,292 --> 00:03:05,144
If you want a quiet moment before dinner

81
00:03:05,144 --> 00:03:08,567
step into one of Insadong's traditional tea houses.

82
00:03:08,567 --> 00:03:11,305
Try a herbal tea like jujube or citron

83
00:03:11,305 --> 00:03:14,172
and enjoy a slower side of the city.

84
00:03:14,502 --> 00:03:17,822
Finish with an evening walk along Cheonggyecheon

85
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:20,202
the stream that runs below street level from

86
00:03:20,202 --> 00:03:21,882
Cheonggye Plaza.

87
00:03:21,882 --> 00:03:23,622
It's lit up after dark

88
00:03:23,622 --> 00:03:24,742
it's free

89
00:03:24,742 --> 00:03:26,822
and it's an easy way to end a long

90
00:03:26,822 --> 00:03:27,742
first day.

91
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:30,800
Day two is for food

92
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,940
shopping and the best view of the city.

93
00:03:33,906 --> 00:03:35,869
Start at Gwangjang Market

94
00:03:35,869 --> 00:03:38,591
near Jongno 5-ga Station on Line 1.

95
00:03:38,591 --> 00:03:42,137
It's one of Seoul's oldest markets and a great

96
00:03:42,137 --> 00:03:45,050
place for breakfast or an early lunch.

97
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:46,632
Look for bindaetteok

98
00:03:46,632 --> 00:03:50,621
a crispy mung bean pancake fried right at the stall

99
00:03:50,621 --> 00:03:51,951
and mayak gimbap

100
00:03:51,951 --> 00:03:55,560
little rice rolls that are hard to stop eating.

101
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:58,266
Bring some cash for the stalls.

102
00:03:58,716 --> 00:04:02,776
Then take the subway to Myeongdong on Line 4.

103
00:04:02,776 --> 00:04:06,176
It's packed with cosmetics shops and fashion stores

104
00:04:06,176 --> 00:04:09,896
and from late afternoon the street food stalls open.

105
00:04:09,896 --> 00:04:12,816
Many shops offer tax refunds for visitors

106
00:04:12,816 --> 00:04:15,256
so bring your passport when you go shopping.

107
00:04:15,726 --> 00:04:17,546
From late afternoon

108
00:04:17,546 --> 00:04:20,706
Myeongdong's main streets fill with food stalls.

109
00:04:20,706 --> 00:04:21,806
Grilled skewers

110
00:04:21,806 --> 00:04:22,746
egg bread

111
00:04:22,746 --> 00:04:24,906
sweet pancakes called hotteok.

112
00:04:24,906 --> 00:04:26,686
Most stalls take cards now

113
00:04:26,686 --> 00:04:28,986
but keep a little cash just in case

114
00:04:28,986 --> 00:04:30,806
and look for the price on the sign before

115
00:04:30,806 --> 00:04:31,566
you order.

116
00:04:32,376 --> 00:04:34,516
As the sun goes down

117
00:04:34,516 --> 00:04:37,676
go up Namsan to N Seoul Tower.

118
00:04:37,676 --> 00:04:40,216
From Myeongdong you can walk to the cable car

119
00:04:40,216 --> 00:04:43,036
or take a bus up the mountain.

120
00:04:43,036 --> 00:04:45,856
The view is best around sunset.

121
00:04:45,856 --> 00:04:48,056
Cable car and observatory times change with

122
00:04:48,056 --> 00:04:48,696
the season

123
00:04:48,696 --> 00:04:50,616
so check them that morning.

124
00:04:51,378 --> 00:04:54,038
Day three is yours.

125
00:04:54,038 --> 00:04:56,558
Each of these options fills about half a day

126
00:04:56,558 --> 00:04:57,758
so pick two.

127
00:04:58,236 --> 00:05:00,136
Want more history?

128
00:05:00,136 --> 00:05:03,236
Visit Changdeokgung Palace and its Secret Garden.

129
00:05:03,236 --> 00:05:04,976
The garden can only be seen on a guided

130
00:05:04,976 --> 00:05:06,736
tour with its own ticket

131
00:05:06,736 --> 00:05:08,176
and places are limited

132
00:05:08,176 --> 00:05:09,136
so book ahead.

133
00:05:09,606 --> 00:05:12,186
Into design and shopping?

134
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:13,926
Go to Dongdaemun Design Plaza

135
00:05:13,926 --> 00:05:17,166
and the fashion malls around Dongdaemun that

136
00:05:17,166 --> 00:05:18,466
stay open late.

137
00:05:19,056 --> 00:05:21,956
Want to slow down like a local?

138
00:05:21,956 --> 00:05:24,216
Spend the afternoon in a Han River park

139
00:05:24,216 --> 00:05:25,976
like Yeouido.

140
00:05:25,976 --> 00:05:27,476
People picnic

141
00:05:27,476 --> 00:05:30,696
cycle and order fried chicken to the riverbank.

142
00:05:30,696 --> 00:05:31,936
Renting a bike is easy

143
00:05:31,936 --> 00:05:34,376
and there's always a convenience store nearby.

144
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:38,450
Or relax properly at a jjimjilbang

145
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:40,310
a Korean bathhouse.

146
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:42,090
It's one of the most local things you can

147
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:43,330
do in Seoul.

148
00:05:43,330 --> 00:05:45,790
Just read up on the etiquette before you go.

149
00:05:46,332 --> 00:05:49,312
And if you have more than three days

150
00:05:49,312 --> 00:05:51,472
explore neighbourhoods like Seongsu

151
00:05:51,472 --> 00:05:53,132
Hongdae or Itaewon

152
00:05:53,132 --> 00:05:55,772
or take a day trip out of the city

153
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:58,172
like Suwon's Hwaseong Fortress

154
00:05:58,172 --> 00:05:59,912
an easy train ride away.

155
00:06:00,294 --> 00:06:04,114
Almost everything in this plan is on the subway.

156
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:05,574
Tap your card in and out at the gates

157
00:06:05,574 --> 00:06:07,914
and use the same card on buses.

158
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:13,364
Seoul's subway is easy for visitors.

159
00:06:13,364 --> 00:06:15,524
Lines have numbers and colours

160
00:06:15,524 --> 00:06:16,964
station names are in English

161
00:06:16,964 --> 00:06:19,124
and announcements are in English too.

162
00:06:19,124 --> 00:06:20,704
When you change lines

163
00:06:20,704 --> 00:06:23,004
just follow the colour of the line you want.

164
00:06:23,706 --> 00:06:27,507
Taxis are easy to find and fair for short trips.

165
00:06:27,507 --> 00:06:29,247
With the Kakao T app

166
00:06:29,247 --> 00:06:33,026
you can book one without speaking any Korean.

167
00:06:33,324 --> 00:06:34,282
Before you go

168
00:06:34,282 --> 00:06:37,208
here are four small mistakes that catch a lot

169
00:06:37,208 --> 00:06:38,944
of first-time visitors.

170
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:41,072
One.

171
00:06:41,072 --> 00:06:42,536
Palaces on a weekend.

172
00:06:42,536 --> 00:06:46,254
Most sights are busiest on weekends and public holidays

173
00:06:46,254 --> 00:06:49,239
so do the palaces on a weekday if you can.

174
00:06:49,239 --> 00:06:49,577
Two.

175
00:06:49,577 --> 00:06:51,210
Lunch after two o'clock.

176
00:06:51,210 --> 00:06:54,027
Many restaurants close for a break in the

177
00:06:54,027 --> 00:06:55,660
middle of the afternoon

178
00:06:55,660 --> 00:06:57,012
so eat lunch early.

179
00:06:57,012 --> 00:06:57,462
Three.

180
00:06:57,462 --> 00:06:59,039
No cash at the market.

181
00:06:59,039 --> 00:07:00,954
Cards work almost everywhere

182
00:07:00,954 --> 00:07:03,827
but carry a little cash for market stalls.

183
00:07:03,827 --> 00:07:04,503
And four.

184
00:07:04,503 --> 00:07:06,305
Trusting old opening hours.

185
00:07:06,305 --> 00:07:08,333
Hours and closing days change

186
00:07:08,333 --> 00:07:10,924
so check each place on a map app the

187
00:07:10,924 --> 00:07:12,294
morning you go.

188
00:07:12,936 --> 00:07:15,216
And one bonus tip.

189
00:07:15,216 --> 00:07:18,616
Convenience stores are your best friend in Seoul.

190
00:07:18,616 --> 00:07:20,996
They're on almost every corner

191
00:07:20,996 --> 00:07:22,796
many are open around the clock

192
00:07:22,796 --> 00:07:24,676
and you can buy water

193
00:07:24,676 --> 00:07:25,896
snacks and a quick meal

194
00:07:25,896 --> 00:07:28,556
and top up your transit card with cash.

195
00:07:28,890 --> 00:07:31,810
A few questions people often ask.

196
00:07:31,810 --> 00:07:34,550
Is three days enough for Seoul?

197
00:07:34,550 --> 00:07:36,890
It covers the main palaces

198
00:07:36,890 --> 00:07:38,510
a traditional market

199
00:07:38,510 --> 00:07:40,490
a shopping street and a city view

200
00:07:40,490 --> 00:07:42,350
at a comfortable pace.

201
00:07:42,756 --> 00:07:45,636
Which day should you visit Gyeongbokgung?

202
00:07:45,636 --> 00:07:47,536
Any day except Tuesday

203
00:07:47,536 --> 00:07:49,076
when it's closed.

204
00:07:49,076 --> 00:07:51,216
Weekday mornings are the quietest.

205
00:07:51,726 --> 00:07:54,166
Do you need to book anything?

206
00:07:54,166 --> 00:07:57,126
Most of this plan needs no booking at all.

207
00:07:57,126 --> 00:08:00,106
The one exception is the Secret Garden tour at

208
00:08:00,106 --> 00:08:01,186
Changdeokgung

209
00:08:01,186 --> 00:08:03,506
which has limited places.

210
00:08:03,506 --> 00:08:06,346
Popular restaurants can also have queues at

211
00:08:06,346 --> 00:08:07,366
busy times.

212
00:08:07,776 --> 00:08:10,256
So that's three days in Seoul.

213
00:08:10,256 --> 00:08:11,896
Day one, palaces

214
00:08:11,896 --> 00:08:13,756
hanok lanes and the stream.

215
00:08:13,756 --> 00:08:14,536
Day two

216
00:08:14,536 --> 00:08:15,956
a market breakfast

217
00:08:15,956 --> 00:08:18,336
Myeongdong and the sunset from Namsan.

218
00:08:18,336 --> 00:08:19,236
Day three

219
00:08:19,236 --> 00:08:20,436
whatever you love most.

220
00:08:20,946 --> 00:08:22,246
The full plan

221
00:08:22,246 --> 00:08:24,046
with links for every stop

222
00:08:24,046 --> 00:08:25,946
is on Korea Plainly.

223
00:08:25,946 --> 00:08:28,166
The link is in the description.

224
00:08:28,166 --> 00:08:29,666
If this helped

225
00:08:29,666 --> 00:08:31,306
subscribe for more plain

226
00:08:31,306 --> 00:08:33,226
practical guides to Korea.

227
00:08:33,226 --> 00:08:35,046
Have a wonderful trip to Seoul.

